  ],
  "implementation": {
    "geometry": "H64,D512=(C448,R64),group-major output[8,rows,4096],V is K. CUDA SM80+ tensor-core implementation with sufficient opt-in shared memory; qualification hardware is the designated SM120 GPU.",
    "ownership": "Immutable F32[1,64] raw sink handle belongs to backend model. All activation, pool, frequency, index, output and scratch views belong to one caller request. No GPU handles added to CPU model weights; no model-family logic added to transformer/provider bridge.",
    "window": "Attend newest-first over the PRE-update sliding ring and current rotated KV chunk, clipped by shared floor. Then attend pool entries in source order, without deduplicating overlapping window/pool contributions. This operation does not update rings or advance positions.",
    "pool": "Dense per-row bound=min(floor((pos0+row+1)/rate),entries), or512 gathered logical IDs with -1 padding and caller-guaranteed valid/causal IDs. Immutable page table maps valid IDs to split F16 C/R pools. Empty pools/ring/current-chunk/unused scratch require canonical empty views where unused.",
    "execution": "Source auto split8/16 when rows<=8, based on estimated visible contributions; otherwise one-shot32-head tiles. Split16-head partials write explicit F32 m/l and numerator workspace, then combine with learned sink. No hidden scratch allocation, host transfer, internal fence or state commit.",
    "arithmetic": "Latent dot (including explicit padded zeros) then RoPE dot, scale1/sqrt512. Online FP32 exp/normalizer, source-ordered reduction, F16 probabilities BEFORE tensor-core value product. Prior accumulators are scaled BEFORE MMA. F32 division and source-contracted de-rotation precede final F16 store.",
    "optimizations": "Precompute physical key addresses once per tile, power-of-two page shifts, aligned128-bit loads with scalar fallback, ldmatrix/shared matrix operands, register accumulators, parallel four-lane-per-head softmax preserving original sum order, shared scratch padding, split-combine merge reused across eight output pairs per thread, cached one-shot trigonometry/denominators.",
    "preflight": "Dimensions, positions, window/history capacity, physical pool capacity, exact counts/types, request identity, canonical empty views, sink owner/type/shape and pairwise overlap validated before enqueue. Malformed late metadata rejects without output writes. CUDA execution errors mark request failed."
  },
